--- body ---
## Context

Tracker 0406, step S4. After S3, `experiments/Makefile` holds only P1
sweep verbs (census, regimes, decomposed, verification, sourced,
frontier — money-gated API runs) and corpus utils (pdf2md, build-corpus,
preflight, help), plus one P2-delegating alias (`census-summary`,
explicitly deferred to this step by S3 review). S4 renames it to
`experiments/acquire.mk`, applies the header contract, and adds the
mechanical guard for the P1 invariant: every target is .PHONY (manually
invoked, money-gated; no file target downstream can depend on).

## Design (ratified, tracker 0406)

- `experiments/acquire.mk` = P1. Sources: `experiments.toml`, corpus.
  Outcomes: raw replies under `experiments/outputs/**`, `archive/**`
  (tracked by the 0405 policy). NO file targets — every target .PHONY.
- Header contract: phase (P1 acquire), sources, outcomes, invariant
  ("every target is .PHONY; nothing downstream may depend on a P1
  target as a file"), and the money-gate warning (sweeps cost API
  dollars; test-one-before-blasting).
- **census-summary alias: DROP it.** P1 may not carry a cross-phase
  delegation edge (root's two-entry rule arrives in S5; the documented
  dev path is calling score.mk directly). Sweep call sites first:
  root Makefile l.137 (`$(MAKE) -C experiments census`) is the CENSUS
  sweep (P1, different from census-summary) — leave its semantics,
  repoint its invocation to acquire.mk. Grep for census-summary
  callers (CI, docs, scripts) and repoint them to
  `make -f experiments/derived/score.mk census-summary` or its
  equivalent target there.
- Guard: `tests/test_acquire_all_phony.py` (@pytest.mark.adherence) —
  parse acquire.mk (and its includes if any, excluding paths.mk vars):
  every rule target is declared .PHONY; zero rules whose target is a
  filesystem path (no `/` in target names is a reasonable first
  needle; refine against the actual file). Also assert no rule writes
  outside experiments/ (no `../` targets).
- After the rename, `make -C experiments` no longer finds a default
  Makefile — that is intended (per-phase .mks are the dev path).
  Repoint every reference; the phase .mk invocation convention is
  `make -f experiments/acquire.mk <sweep>`.

## Relevant files

- `experiments/Makefile` — becomes acquire.mk (git mv + header edits)
- root `Makefile` — l.137 `$(MAKE) -C experiments census` and any other
  `-C experiments` delegations repoint to `-f experiments/acquire.mk`
  (check UV_RUN/.env handling still reaches the sweeps — they make API
  calls and need the env)
- `tests/test_score_build_no_acquire.py` — docstrings/comments
  reference experiments/Makefile (l.5, 13, 107, 124); update wording
  and any needle lists
- `tests/test_makefile_dag.py` and other tests scanning Makefiles —
  ensure acquire.mk is picked up (or deliberately excluded) per each
  test's purpose
- `docs/pipeline-phases.md` — P1 rows reference experiments/Makefile
  (l.15, 23); update to acquire.mk
- `.github/workflows/`, `README.md`, `scripts/` — sweep
  `grep -rn "experiments/Makefile\|-C experiments" --exclude-dir=.git .`

## Actions

1. Red test first: `tests/test_acquire_all_phony.py` — red today
   (file experiments/acquire.mk absent; write it to target acquire.mk
   so it fails on missing file, green after the rename + cleanup).
2. `git mv experiments/Makefile experiments/acquire.mk`; add header
   contract; drop census-summary (repoint callers to score.mk).
3. Repoint all references (root Makefile, tests, docs, CI, README).
4. Verify every remaining target is .PHONY; fix any stragglers found
   by the guard (decide per target: it is either a P1 verb → .PHONY,
   or it does not belong in acquire.mk → relocate, flag in PR).
5. Update docs/pipeline-phases.md.

## Test

The guard test of action 1. Existing gates that must stay green:
test_score_build_no_acquire, test_render_build_clean_room,
test_makefile_dag, both P4 clean-room tests,
test_no_tracked_ignored_files.

## Verification

- [ ] `grep -rn "experiments/Makefile" --exclude-dir=.git .` → zero in
      Makefiles/tests/CI/docs (tickets history OK)
- [ ] Guard test green: all acquire.mk targets .PHONY, no path targets
- [ ] `make check` green; `make report` / `make slides` build; CI green
- [ ] Sweep verbs still resolve in dry-run:
      `make -f experiments/acquire.mk -n census` (NEVER for real —
      money gate)

## Invariants

- No artifact content changes; NEVER run sweeps for real (API cost)
- score.mk / render.mk untouched except reference wording
- One PR, this child only; tracker 0406 stays open

## Exit criteria

- experiments/acquire.mk exists (header contract, all-.PHONY,
  money-gate doc); experiments/Makefile gone
- census-summary alias dropped, callers repointed
- Guard test enforces the P1 invariant mechanically
